{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a15341-8a18-73d7-a97a-a283b94ce4cb","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/built-in/contracts/SKILL.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\nsrc/App.tsx` (boilerplate in `references/contract-deploy.md`).\\n   246\\t- Everything else — including \\\"create/build/deploy a token/NFT/contract\\\" with no UI ask → do NOT touch `App.tsx`. Confirm the deploy in one short sentence and mention the artifact and metadata paths, then stop. Do NOT restate the raw address, tx hash, or explorer URL in prose — the chat timeline renders a contract card with all three from the deploy_contract result, and the Workbench's Contracts panel surfaces the deployment. If a UI would help, OFFER it in one sentence — never build one unprompted \\\"to be helpful\\\".\\n   247\\t\\n   248\\t## Hard rules (re-read before every contract action)\\n   249\\t\\n   250\\t- Default to a balanced review; never ask which review level to use. The only mid-thread questions allowed are the re-engagement points in \\\"Surfacing a finding or tradeoff\\\". This governs the review level and mid-flow interruptions only — it does NOT suppress the up-front requirements clarification that runs before STEP 1 when your mode calls for it (see \\\"Before STEP 1\\\" above).\\n   251\\t- Call it a \\\"review\\\", never an \\\"audit\\\", in everything the user sees.\\n   252\\t- The five subagents are siblings — never ask any of them to call `task()` (they have no subagents). Auditors are read-only; testers are read-only on contract source (they author test files only).\\n   253\\t- Always pass `severity level: <quick|balanced|max>` in every auditor `task()` description.\\n   254\\t- Always dispatch both auditors in the SAME assistant turn.\\n   255\\t- Never tell the user an auditor ran, or report its `## Audit Provenance` row, unless you actually dispatched it via `task(subagent_type=...)` in this turn and read that row back from its own report.\\n   256\\t- The audit-level severity governs ONLY the audit's tier and round-cap — it does NOT auto-trigger Slither or unit tests (those are gated by the preset's tool slots). Integration tests are never auto-run by any preset.\\n   257\\t- Never auto-run POST-deploy integration tests (STEP 8, Mode 1 / plain Mode 2). After a successful deploy, offer them in one sentence and run only if the user accepts. STEP 6's pre-deploy VERIFY-ON-FORK gate (Compass-engine Mode 2) is the one exception — it always runs, in every preset, and is not an offer.\\n   258\\t- Never pass `--mode live` to `compass:deploy` unless STEP 6's gate ran and passed this session. Otherwise omit `--mode` and let `fork-then-live` rehearse — and know that on a contract with constructor args that rehearsal cannot run, so it degrades to the script's arg preflight (see STEP 7).\\n   259\\t- Initial writes always go to `contract-writer`. Big rewrites and multi-finding fixes also go to the writer.\\n   260\\t- Always read `references/contract-deploy.md` in full before any deploy (and the matching mode file in full once you've picked a mode); read `references/static-analysis.md` in full before running Slither.\\n   261\\t- Always run STEP 3a (preview) before STEP 3b (apply).\\n   262\\t- Never silently move past unresolved Critical / High findings, unresolved Slither findings, unresolved test failures, or unresolved live-behaviour discrepancies.\\n   263\\t- \\\"Deploy it anyway\\\" and any equivalent phrase is NOT consent to fix + deploy. When the user expresses deploy intent alongside an unresolved Critical/High finding, surface the binary choice per \\\"Surfacing a finding or tradeoff\\\" (deploy as-is with known risk, OR fix first then deploy) and wait for explicit selection. Never choose either path autonomously.\\n   264\\t- Stay on balanced unless an unambiguous keyword switches to quick or max.\\n   265\\t- Never build a frontend/UI unless the original request explicitly asked for an app/UI/page/demo — contract + deploy is the default deliverable. Do not infer UI intent from \\\"create/build a token/contract\\\".\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01AK4fzsAxL2NA2D4KNuz5y8\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.12\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a15341-8a1d-732a-a674-5e49e600539c","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/AGENTS.md","limit":200},"result":"{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"status\":\"success\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"     1\\t# [App Name]\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t> Built with Arc Studio - money-powered apps in minutes\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\tThis is the **project memory** - what Arc Studio remembers about building this app. It helps future agents (or humans) understand and extend the project.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t---\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t## What This App Does\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\t[Brief description of what the app does and its primary use case]\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\t## Tech Stack\\n    14\\t\\n    15\\t- Frontend: React 18, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS\\n    16\\t- Web3: wagmi v2, viem v2, ConnectKit\\n    17\\t- Contracts: Solidity 0.8.28 + Foundry. Sources in `contracts/`, unit tests in `contracts/test/*.t.sol`. Build with `bun run contracts:build` (`forge build`), test with `bun run contracts:test` (`forge test`).\\n    18\\t- Wallet: injected (MetaMask, etc.)\\n    19\\t- Chain: Arc Testnet (Chain ID: 5042002, imported from `viem/chains`)\\n    20\\t- Token: USDC (6 decimals) (Address: 0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000, Chain: Arc Testnet)\\n    21\\t- Toasts: Sonner\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t## Key Files\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\t- `src/App.tsx` - Main application logic\\n    26\\t- `src/components/` - UI components\\n    27\\t- `src/config.ts` - wagmi config (chains, connectors, transports)\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t## To Run\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t```bash\\n    32\\tbun install\\n    33\\tbun run dev\\n    34\\t```\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_019ctHCGRZaWS5tFuDSc2LWt\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.12\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
