{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"running","toolCallId":"01a15341-a981-753d-9e13-fd86e983a450","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/built-in/contracts/references/contract-deploy.md","limit":2000}}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a15341-a981-753d-9e13-fd86e983a450","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/built-in/contracts/references/contract-deploy.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\ny) fails, you get **exactly one** retry before surfacing the failure to the user. Use that retry slot to actually fix the problem when you can — don't burn it on a blind rerun unless the error is plainly transient.\\n   107\\t\\n   108\\tWorkflow:\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\t1. **Read the error carefully.** Look at the full message returned by the tool (revert reason, validation error, RPC error, faucet error). Don't paraphrase or guess — the error usually tells you exactly what's wrong.\\n   111\\t2. **Classify the error and act:**\\n   112\\t   - **Transient** (RPC timeout, 5xx, \\\"please try again\\\", \\\"transaction underpriced\\\", intermittent Circle API hiccup, faucet rate limit) → retry the same call once with the same parameters. No source change needed.\\n   113\\t   - **Debuggable / fixable** (constructor revert with a real reason like \\\"ZeroAddress\\\" / \\\"InvalidFee\\\", `require` / custom-error revert, obvious bad constructor arg, stale artifact after a source edit, missing/wrong owner address, bytecode-size limit, etc.) → diagnose first, then fix the underlying cause, THEN retry. Examples:\\n   114\\t     - Constructor reverted on a zero-address check → pass a real address (likely the deployer wallet — see \\\"Owner / Admin Constructor Args\\\" above).\\n   115\\t     - Constructor reverted on a value range / invariant → pass an arg that satisfies the invariant.\\n   116\\t     - Stale artifact (you edited the `.sol` after the writer last built) → rebuild (`cd /home/user/app && forge build`), then redeploy.\\n   117\\t     - Source-level bug surfaced by the revert → if the fix is a single small one, apply it directly + rebuild; if it's non-trivial, re-delegate to `contract-writer` before retrying. The writer round-trip is allowed — it does NOT count as the deploy retry.\\n   118\\t   - **Non-transient and not fixable from here** (invalid contract name, missing artifact you can't regenerate, missing platform credentials) → do NOT retry. Surface the error to the user with a one-line explanation and a suggested next step.\\n   119\\t3. **One retry only.** After fixing the cause (or accepting it's transient), call the deploy tool ONE more time. Do NOT auto-retry again.\\n   120\\t4. **If the retry also fails**, surface BOTH errors to the user (initial + retry), state what you tried in between, and ask whether they want to try again, switch deployment modes (Mode 1 ↔ Mode 2), or abandon. NEVER silently loop.\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\tMode-specific retry rules layer on top of this — see `./self-deploy.md` \\\"Retry on failure\\\" for the self-deploy buckets (faucet, transient, constructor revert).\\n   123\\t\\n   124\\t## Wire Into App\\n   125\\t\\n   126\\t1. Check `/home/user/app/contracts/contract-metadata/<ContractName>.json`:\\n   127\\t  - Ensure it includes:\\n   128\\t    - `contract_code_path`\\n   129\\t    - `contract_compiled_code_path`\\n   130\\t    - `contract_network_and_links` (network -> explorer link map)\\n   131\\t2. Read the ABI from the Foundry artifact and create a contracts config:\\n   132\\t\\n   133\\t```typescript\\n   134\\timport artifact from \\\"../../contracts/out/SimpleToken.sol/SimpleToken.json\\\";\\n   135\\t\\n   136\\texport const SIMPLE_TOKEN = {\\n   137\\t  address: \\\"0x742d35Cc6634C0532925a3b844Bc9e7595f8fE21\\\" as const,\\n   138\\t  abi: artifact.abi,\\n   139\\t};\\n   140\\t```\\n   141\\t\\n   142\\t3. Confirm the deploy in one short sentence and suggest trying the main action — do NOT restate the raw address, tx hash, or explorer URL in prose (the chat timeline renders a contract card with all three from the deploy_contract result). If they need testnet USDC or gas to interact, tell them to use Arc Studio's built-in **Get test USDC** (sidebar button) — do not send them to faucet.circle.com or other external faucets for their own try-it flow. In-app faucet links you embed in the preview are fine.\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_019uvj3q4op7eJBQjEp4KeWM\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.12\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
